* Sat Apr 11 2026 Weilin Tong <tongweilin@linux.alibaba.com> [6.6.102-5.4_rc1%%DIST%%]
- anolis: mm: vmscan: add writeback throttling if reclaim cannot make progress (Baolin Wang)
- mm/vmscan: unify writeback reclaim statistic and throttling (Kairui Song)
- mm/vmscan: remove sc->unqueued_dirty (Kairui Song)
- mm/vmscan: remove sc->file_taken (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: remove no longer used reclaim argument for folio protection (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: simplify and improve dirty writeback handling (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: use the common routine for dirty/writeback reactivation (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: remove redundant swap constrained check upon isolation (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: don't abort scan immediately right after aging (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: use a smaller batch for reclaim (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: scan and count the exact number of folios (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: restructure the reclaim loop (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: relocate the LRU scan batch limit to callers (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: rename variables related to aging and rotation (Kairui Song)
- mm/mglru: consolidate common code for retrieving evictable size (Kairui Song)
- mm: vmscan: fix dirty folios throttling on cgroup v1 for MGLRU (Baolin Wang)
- mm: vmscan: apply proportional reclaim pressure for memcg when MGLRU is enabled (Koichiro Den)
- anolis: mm: support min_cache_kbytes when mglru enabled (Kaihao Bai)
- anolis: mm: fix MGLRU's batch mode for scanning page tables (Baolin Wang)
- mm/rmap: fix incorrect pte restoration for lazyfree folios (Dev Jain)
- arm64: mm: fix using the incorrect pte_cont() to check contiguous PTEs (Baolin Wang)
- anolis: arm64: mm: implement the architecture-specific test_and_clear_young_ptes() (Baolin Wang)
- anolis: mm: support batched checking of the young flag for MGLRU (Baolin Wang)
- anolis: mm: add a batched helper to clear the young flag for large folios (Baolin Wang)
- anolis: mm: use inline helper functions instead of ugly macros (Baolin Wang)
- mm: rmap: skip batched unmapping for UFFD vmas (Baolin Wang)
- anolis: configs: enable CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_HW_PTE_YOUNG and CONFIG_LRU_GEN_WALKS_MMU (Baolin Wang)
- mm/mglru: fix PTE-mapped large folios (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: rework workingset protection (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: rework refault detection (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: rework type selection (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: rework aging feedback (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: optimize deactivation (Yu Zhao)
- Revert "mm/gup: clear the LRU flag of a page before adding to LRU batch" (Hugh Dickins)
- mm/mglru: clean up workingset (Yu Zhao)
- mm: add defines for min/max swappiness (Dan Schatzberg)
- mm/mglru: improve swappiness handling (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: improve struct lru_gen_mm_walk (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: improve reset_mm_stats() (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: improve should_run_aging() (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: drop unused parameter (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: remove CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: add dummy pmd_dirty() (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: remove CONFIG_MEMCG (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: add CONFIG_LRU_GEN_WALKS_MMU (Kinsey Ho)
- mm/mglru: add CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_HW_PTE_YOUNG (Kinsey Ho)
- mm: multi-gen LRU: ignore non-leaf pmd_young for force_scan=true (Yuanchu Xie)
- mm: rmap: support batched unmapping for file large folios (Baolin Wang)
- arm64: mm: implement the architecture-specific clear_flush_young_ptes() (Baolin Wang)
- arm64: mm: support batch clearing of the young flag for large folios (Baolin Wang)
- arm64: mm: factor out the address and ptep alignment into a new helper (Baolin Wang)
- mm: rmap: support batched checks of the references for large folios (Baolin Wang)
- mm: multi-gen LRU: use {ptep,pmdp}_clear_young_notify() (Yu Zhao)
- mm: multi-gen LRU: remove MM_LEAF_OLD and MM_NONLEAF_TOTAL stats (Yu Zhao)
- mm/mglru: reset page lru tier bits when activating (Wei Xu)
- mm/rmap: fix a mlock race condition in folio_referenced_one() (Kiryl Shutsemau)
- mm/page_vma_mapped: track if the page is mapped across page table boundary (Kiryl Shutsemau)
- mm/rmap: fix potential out-of-bounds page table access during batched unmap (Lance Yang)
- mm: support batched unmap for lazyfree large folios during reclamation (Barry Song)
- mm: support tlbbatch flush for a range of PTEs (Barry Song)
- arm64: tlb: Allow range operation for MAX_TLBI_RANGE_PAGES (Gavin Shan)
- mm: set folio swapbacked iff folios are dirty in try_to_unmap_one (Barry Song)
- mm/rmap: remove duplicated exit code in pagewalk loop (Lance Yang)
- mm: vmscan: simplify the logic for activating dirty file folios (Baolin Wang)
- mm: vmscan: filter out the dirty file folios for node_reclaim() (Baolin Wang)
- mm/mremap: honour writable bit in mremap pte batching (Dev Jain)
- mm: introduce FPB_RESPECT_WRITE for PTE batching infrastructure (Dev Jain)
- mm: remove boolean output parameters from folio_pte_batch_ext() (David Hildenbrand)
- mm: split folio_pte_batch() into folio_pte_batch() and folio_pte_batch_flags() (David Hildenbrand)
- mm: smaller folio_pte_batch() improvements (David Hildenbrand)
- mm: convert FPB_IGNORE_* into FPB_RESPECT_* (David Hildenbrand)
- mm/mlock: implement folio_mlock_step() using folio_pte_batch() (Lance Yang)
- mm: fix folio_pte_batch() on XEN PV (Petr Vaněk)

